# ── MARK LVI — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
#
# NOTHING BELOW MAY CARRY A TRAILING COMMENT. Gitignore has no inline comments:
# `path   # why` is read as one file name whose text includes the `#`, so the
# rule matches nothing. This block said exactly that for its whole life and
# `config/api_keys.json` was tracked as a result; `tests/test_gitignore.py` now
# fails the build if a rule here stops matching.
#
# Your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials.
config/api_keys.json
# The dashboard's TLS private key and certificate.
config/certs/
# A LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your account.
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins).
**/token*.json
# Temporary OAuth token during an atomic save.
config/.calendar-token-*
# The action audit log: names files and decisions the user made.
config/audit.jsonl
# Today's suggestion count; meaningless once committed.
config/suggestions.json
# Google OAuth client secrets.
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
# Piper voices: 63 MB per voice, downloaded on first use. They live inside
# providers/ so that deleting providers/ takes them with it — which is also why
# they have to be named here or `git add providers/` swallows them.
providers/voices/

# Encrypted browser credentials, SQLite journals, and interprocess lock
memory/browser_vault.db*

# ── Coverage output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.coverage` is a SQLite file full of absolute paths from whichever machine ran
# the suite. It was committed once by accident and then looked like a source
# file to every `git status` afterwards.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# A hang report written next to the log; it is evidence, not source.
hang.txt
